 11:29; 20:12). This name was given to her at the time that it was announced to Abraham that she should be the mother of the promised child.","verses":48,"father":"Terah","mother":"","v":[9]},{"id":"israel_682","name":"Israel","also":"","summary":"One who follows on another’s heels; supplanter, (Gen. 25:26; 27:36; Hos. 12:2-4), the second born of the twin sons of Isaac by Rebekah. He was born probably at Lahai-roi, when his father was fifty-nine and Abraham one hundred and fifty-nine years old.","verses":1009,"father":"Isaac","mother":"Rebekah","v":[13,27]},{"id":"esau_1216","name":"Esau","also":"Edom, Edomite","summary":"Hairy, Rebekah’s first-born twin son (Gen. 25:25). The name of Edom, “red”, was also given to him from his conduct in connection with the red lentil “pottage” for which he sold his birthright (30, 31).","verses":151,"father":"Isaac","mother":"Rebekah","v":[13]},{"id":"moses_2108","name":"Moses","also":"","summary":"Drawn (or Egypt. mesu, “son;” hence Rameses, royal son). On the invitation of Pharaoh (Gen. 45:17-25), Jacob and his sons went down into Egypt.","verses":774,"father":"Amram","mother":"Jochebed","v":[15]},{"id":"pharaoh_2331","name":"Pharaoh","also":"","summary":"The Pharaoh of the Exodus was probably Menephtah I., the fourteenth and eldest surviving son of Rameses II. He resided at Zoan, where he had the various interviews with Moses and Aaron recorded in the book of Exodus.","verses":138,"father":"","mother":"","v":[17]},{"id":"hosea_1555","name":"Hosea","also":"Osee","summary":"Salvation, the son of Beeri, and author of the book of prophecies bearing his name. He belonged to the kingdom of Israel. “His Israelitish origin is attested by the peculiar, rough, Aramaizing diction, pointing to the northern part of Palestine; by the intimate acquaintance he evinces with the localities of Ephraim (5:1; 6:8, 9; 12:12; 14:6, etc.); by passages like 1:2, where the kingdom is styled ‘the land’, and 7:5, where the Israelitish king is designated as ‘our’ king.”","verses":3,"father":"Beeri","mother":"","v":[25]},{"id":"isaiah_617","name":"Isaiah","also":"Esaias","summary":"The son of Amoz (Isa. 1:1; 2:1), who was apparently a man of humble rank. His wife was called “the prophetess” (8:3), either because she was endowed with the prophetic gift, like Deborah (Judg. 4:4) and Huldah (2 Kings 22:14-20), or simply because she was the wife of “the prophet” (Isa. 38:1).","verses":53,"father":"Amoz","mother":"","v":[27,29]}],"places":[{"id":"gomorrah_489","name":"Gomorrah","kind":"City","lat":31.15725,"lon":35.47395,"summary":"Submersion, one of the five cities of the plain of Siddim which were destroyed by fire (Gen. 10:19; 13:10; 19:24, 28). These cities probably stood close together, and were near the northern extremity of what is now the Dead Sea.","verses":23,"v":[29]},{"id":"sodom_1107","name":"Sodom","kind":"City","lat":31.19656,"lon":35.39648,"summary":"Burning; the walled, a city in the vale of Siddim (Gen. 13:10; 14:1-16). The wickedness of its inhabitants brought down upon it fire from heaven, by which it was destroyed (18:16-33; 19:1-29; Deut. 23:17).","verses":47,"v":[29]},{"id":"zion_1263","name":"Zion","kind":"Mountain","lat":31.77667,"lon":35.23417,"summary":"Sunny; height, one of the eminences on which Jerusalem was built. It was surrounded on all sides, except the north, by deep valleys, that of the Tyropoeon separating it from Moriah, which it surpasses in height by 105 feet.","verses":140,"v":[33]}],"events":[],"traditions":[["election-and-predestination",6,24],["israel-and-the-church",1,8]],"sources":["Barnes","JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[3004,3004,225,225,1722,5547,5574,5574,5574,5574,4828,4828,1473,1473,4893,1722,40,40,4151],[1473,1510,3173,3077,2532,88,3601,3588,1473,2588],[1063,1473,2172,2172,2172,846,846,1510,331,575,575,575,575,5547,5228,5228,5228,5228,1473,80,1473,4773,4773,4773,4773],[3748,3748,3748,2475,3739,3739,3588,5206,5206,5206,2532,3588,1391,1391,2532,3588,1242,2532,3588,35